@schema x.code/v1 { version: 1, relations: [x.code/touches, x.code/exercises] }

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-1 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f4a0deceb63d3ccc703aff259a2d102eada3c26f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Rewrites now always end with a newline }
~ Rewrites now always end with a newline

To ensure that the file is correctly handled by both the queue and the hook, which have different methods of appending to the file.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-2 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "It now goes in the JSON as a `behind` field, and on stdout only in the human-readable mode where it belongs." }
~ `stale --json` now includes the `behind` field in JSON output instead of printing it on stdout

To ensure that `--json` outputs only valid JSON, preventing parsing errors when consuming the JSON output.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-3 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "A test runs every `--json` command in this repository, which records its own commits, and requires the output to parse." }
~ A test is added to ensure that every `--json` command produces valid JSON output

To catch future regressions where non-JSON content might be printed with `--json`, ensuring the output remains valid.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-4 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(mut around) = scope {" }
~ The `facts` function now includes an optional `scope` parameter to filter facts based on files, names, or hops

To provide more granular control over which facts are displayed.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-5 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.estimate {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now estimates the time required for extraction based on commit size and prints …

To give users an idea of how long the extraction process will take, especially when processing multiple commits.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-6 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if dry_run {" }
~ The `extract` function now includes a dry-run mode that simulates the extraction process without actually …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-7 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if let Some(path) = c.prompt_file {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `prompt_file` parameter that allows specifying a custom system …

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-8 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let take = if r.max_commits == 0 {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `max_commits` parameter to limit the number of commits processed

To prevent processing an excessive number of commits at once, which could be resource-intensive.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-9 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let kept = if force {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `force` parameter to force re-extraction of already recorded …

To allow users to re-extract commits that have already been recorded.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-10 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.dry_run {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `dry_run` parameter to simulate the extraction process without …

To allow users to preview what would be extracted without making any changes.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-11 { status: speculative, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.no_corpus_order {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `no_corpus_order` parameter that allows disabling corpus order

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-12 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.queued {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `queued` parameter to handle extraction of commits from a queue

To allow users to extract commits that have been queued, either by the post-commit hook or manually.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-13 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "`--json` must be JSON, and nothing else." }
~ `--json` must be JSON, and nothing else

CI went red on a corpus that had grown enough for the case to arise: `stale --json` printed which decisions each moved item was behind — on stdout, before the JSON — and anything reading the output got `Expecting value: line 1 column 3`.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-14 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "if r.estimate {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now estimates the time required for extraction based on commit size and prints …

To give users an idea of how long the extraction process will take, especially when processing multiple commits, an estimation feature was added.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-15 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let take = if r.max_commits == 0 {" }
~ The `extract_command` function now includes a `max_commits` parameter to limit the number of commits processed …

To prevent processing an excessive number of commits at once, which could be resource-intensive, a `max_commits` parameter was added to limit the number of commits processed.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-16 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let mut settings = Settings {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `no_corpus_order` parameter that allows disabling corpus order …

To provide more flexibility in how the check process is conducted, the `check` function was updated to accept a `no_corpus_order` parameter for disabling corpus order.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-17 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: .smysl/commits/b380a5ca16c9.smy@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "let mut settings = Settings {" }
~ The `check` function now includes an optional `parts` parameter to specify the maximum number of parts for …

To allow users to control how the change is split into parts during the checking process, a `parts` parameter was added to the `check` function.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-18 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f4a0deceb63d3ccc703aff259a2d102eada3c26f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": reading repairs what is already there }
~ Reading repairs what is already there

To handle existing content correctly, reading operations will repair or split lines as necessary to match the expected format.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-19 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f4a0deceb63d3ccc703aff259a2d102eada3c26f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": a line of full-length revisions run together is split back into the shas somebody meant }
~ A line of full-length revisions run together is split back into the shas somebody meant

To correctly interpret and process revision data, lines containing concatenated shas are split back into individual components.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-20 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f4a0deceb63d3ccc703aff259a2d102eada3c26f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": a line that is not a plausible revision is reported and dropped }
~ A line that is not a plausible revision is reported and dropped

To maintain data integrity, lines that do not conform to expected revision formats are identified, reported, and discarded.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-21 { status: cited, source: { kind: doc, ref: git:f4a0deceb63d3ccc703aff259a2d102eada3c26f }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": the commit that made `--json` mean JSON }
~ `--json` now means JSON

To provide clear and consistent output, the `--json` flag is updated to always produce JSON formatted data.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-22 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The Rust files to read: those a commit touched, or the working tree's" }
~ The Rust files to read: those a commit touched, or the working tree's

To accurately reflect changes, the tool reads either the files modified by a specific commit or all files in the working tree.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-23 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": Symlinks are not followed: a link can leave the workspace entirely }
~ Symlinks are not followed

To prevent unintended access outside the workspace, symlinks are ignored during file walks.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-24 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A directory that cannot be read is skipped with a note }
~ A directory that cannot be read is skipped with a note

To handle partial failures gracefully, unreadable directories are skipped and noted.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-25 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "The claim is the recorded unit's own words, not the caller's paraphrase" }
~ The claim is the recorded unit's own words, not the caller's paraphrase

To maintain accuracy and consistency, the tool uses the exact text of the recorded claim rather than any user-provided description.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-26 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": "Nothing here concludes anything: the readings are measurements, and every edge waits for a person" }
~ Nothing here concludes anything

To ensure that evidence collection remains an advisory process, no conclusions are drawn or decisions made based on collected data.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-27 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": The opt-in gate (S1): does a test that claims to verify this claim notice the code changing? }
~ The opt-in gate (S1): does a test that claims to verify this claim notice the code changing?

To validate the relevance of tests, an optional mutation gate is introduced to check if tests detect changes in the code.

@decision d/gf4a0deceb63d-28 { status: cited, source: { kind: file, ref: crates/cargo-smysl/src/commands.rs@f4a0deceb63d }, "code:kind": act, "ingest:quote": A prerequisite the extraction marked normative reaches `ImplementedBy` at most }
~ A prerequisite the extraction marked normative reaches `ImplementedBy` at most

To ensure accurate and relevant data, the tool restricts the retrieval of facts related to prerequisites that are marked as normative.

